**Definition 8.1 (native vector and storage).** Evaluate all prices on one
actual $G_{\rm sel}$ run, including original boot and final continuation
when present. Refine ARC Definition 10.1's disjoint opcode/purpose classes
finitely by mode ingress, parser, acquisition binding, source lookup,
source anchor scan and binding serialization. A helper inherits its caller's
purpose unless an explicit finite CTL changes it. Each actual row belongs
to exactly one $(o,p)$ coordinate. Let $A(n)$ count constructed nonmeter
ordinary cells, $b_{\rm ctl}(n)$ every installed finite control bit, active
or inactive, and $C_\tau(n)$ the actually consumed bits at each site kind
of Definition 3.3. Count current partial material and all retained old/dead
banks, scratch, descriptors, captures, inputs and stage blocks.

For an enabled native row at its actual state let $a_n$ be one for EX or
a single ordinary-boundary constructor and zero otherwise; let $c_n$ be
one for a newly installed finite control bit and zero otherwise. Its
complete increments are

$$
\begin{aligned}
\Delta N_{o,p}&=[(o,p)=(o_n,p_n)],&
\Delta A&=a_n,&\Delta b_{\rm ctl}&=c_n,\\
\Delta C_\tau&=[o_n=\operatorname{IN}_\tau],&
\Delta T&=1,&\Delta F&=2,\\
\Delta S&=8a_n+c_n+8.
\end{aligned}
$$

The last eight bits are this actual row's one meter receipt. Existing-cell
WR/erasure reduces no constructed storage. A disabled attempt is no row
and contributes none of these increments. $S_{\rm irr}$ denotes the fixed
irreducible material before these constructions; initialized material is
never also inserted for free in $S_{\rm irr}$ after being counted in $A$
or $b_{\rm ctl}$.

